# Geometry tier with PBEh-3c as the QM1 method (COMPUTATIONAL.md C8).
#
# Why this method: the ORCA 6.1 manual singles PBEh-3c out for geometries --
# "highly efficient ... performing particularly well in the optimization of
# geometries", and "much better geometries [than HF-3c] ... roughly of
# MP2-quality (or even better for non-covalent structures)". The geometry tier
# needs exactly that, and r2SCAN-3c (def2-mTZVPP) is too expensive for the QM
# region the product requires -- the new bond forms ACROSS the QM/QM2 boundary,
# so the complete bridge across the ring (both ester oxygens and both ester
# carbons) has to come inside the QM region.
#
# Cost caveat, to be measured rather than assumed: PBEh-3c is 42% HF exchange on
# a double-zeta basis (def2-mSVP), so it is NOT the cheapest option. The manual's
# ordering is HF-3c < B97-3c < PBEh-3c, and it does not clearly place PBEh-3c
# below r2SCAN-3c. The wall time from this job is the number that settles it.
#
# System: the 137-atom reduced reactant. The spectator water (water1 = O132 +
# H131 + H139) is removed -- at the verified TS the chain is
#   O136-H135 ... O134(water2) -> O132(water1) -> O130(ketone O)
# and H135 is delivered to water2 while water1's H131 never moves (IRC).
#
# Same QM region (17 atoms, 0-based) and GFN-FF topology as the r2SCAN-3c tier,
# so the only change is the QM1 method.
! QM/XTB PBEh-3c ddCOSMO(Water) opt freq TightSCF

%QMMM
QMATOMS
	{61 64 120 121 122 124 125 126 128 129 130 131 132 133 134 135 136}
END
Charge_total 0
Mult_total 1
AutoFF_QM2_Method GFNFF
END

%geom
Calc_Hess true
Recalc_Hess 50
END

%output jsonpropfile true end

%maxcore 4000

%pal
   nprocs 8
end

* xyzfile 0 1 job.xyz
